## Summary

Add helper functions to interact with the docket-state branch via jj commands.

## Implementation

In `src/commands/status/jj.rs`, add:

```rust
/// Get current jj change-id
pub fn current_change_id() -> Result<String> {
    let output = Command::new("jj")
        .args(["log", "-r", "@", "--no-graph", "-T", "change_id"])
        .output()?;
    Ok(String::from_utf8(output.stdout)?.trim().to_string())
}

/// Check if docket-state bookmark exists
pub fn has_state_branch() -> Result<bool> {
    let output = Command::new("jj")
        .args(["bookmark", "list", "--all"])
        .output()?;
    let stdout = String::from_utf8(output.stdout)?;
    Ok(stdout.lines().any(|l| l.starts_with("docket-state")))
}

/// Read file content from state branch
pub fn read_state_file(path: &str) -> Result<String> {
    let output = Command::new("jj")
        .args(["file", "show", "-r", "docket-state", path])
        .output()?;
    Ok(String::from_utf8(output.stdout)?)
}

/// List files in state branch matching pattern
pub fn list_state_files(pattern: &str) -> Result<Vec<String>> {
    // Use jj file list -r docket-state
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] current_change_id() implemented
- [ ] has_state_branch() implemented
- [ ] read_state_file() implemented
- [ ] list_state_files() implemented
- [ ] Error handling for missing jj/state branch
- [ ] Unit tests

